//==
// # The geometry arena
//
// Layer 1 of the STEP B-rep to mesh design (README.md beside this file). The
// flat tables of curves, parameter-plane curves, pcurves, and surfaces that a
// model's topology indexes into, and three views that make one arena entry a
// value implementing the natural-geometry concepts.
//
// Sections, in order:
//  - The arena
//  - Views of one arena entry

//==
// # The arena

// Every curve and surface of one model, in four tables indexed by CurveIndex,
// Curve2DIndex, PcurveIndex and SurfaceIndex, and the closures layer 3 decided
// at decode. Entries reference each other only by index. Well formed
// (IsWellFormed) when every index is in range, no chain of references returns
// to where it started, and every record has the shape its formula needs; every
// evaluation function requires it.
type GeometrySet
{
    Curves: Array<BrepCurve>;
    Curves2D: Array<BrepCurve2D>;
    Pcurves: Array<Pcurve>;
    Surfaces: Array<BrepSurface>;
    Closures: Array<ClosureMark>;
}

// One closure decided at decode for a record whose formula does not wrap: the
// curve, parameter-plane curve, or surface direction named is closed, its two
// ends (or opposite sides) one point set within the model's length tolerance,
// and its Domain is Closed with the range's length as the period (README,
// "Closure is not periodicity"). Layer 3 decides it, from end coincidence; the
// kernel reads it without a tolerance. A mark on a record whose natural domain
// wraps or is unbounded changes nothing (Law_ClosureMarkNamesBoundedAperiodic
// reports it).
type ClosureMark
    = ClosedCurve(Curve: CurveIndex)
    | ClosedCurve2D(Curve: Curve2DIndex)
    | ClosedSurface(Surface: SurfaceIndex, Direction: SurfaceParameter);

//==
// # Views of one arena entry
//
// The evaluation functions take the arena as receiver, so a BrepCurve alone
// cannot implement an interface whose receiver is the curve (PLATO-PRIMER.md
// A.3). A view pairs the arena with one index; it implements the concept by
// delegating to the arena functions, and a non-STEP geometry can implement the
// same concept directly.

// Curve c of the arena g, as a value.
type ArenaCurve
    implements INaturalCurve3D
{
    Geometry: GeometrySet;
    Curve: CurveIndex;
}

// Parameter-plane curve c of the arena g, as a value.
type ArenaCurve2D
    implements INaturalCurve2D
{
    Geometry: GeometrySet;
    Curve: Curve2DIndex;
}

// Surface s of the arena g, as a value.
type ArenaSurface
    implements INaturalSurface
{
    Geometry: GeometrySet;
    Surface: SurfaceIndex;
}
